---
import { briefings, memo, methodology } from '../../content/briefings';
import { watchlist, watchlistTotal } from '../../content/watchlist';
---
<div class="pt-6 md:pt-12">
  <p class="text-[10px] font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-accent mb-3">GTM Radar</p>
  <h2 class="font-serif text-3xl mb-4">A weekly intelligence briefing on AI-reshaped GTM.</h2>
  <p class="font-serif text-lg text-ink/85 leading-relaxed max-w-[640px]">
    Built for GTM recruiters who need to know which companies just raised, who's moving, and what to say in outreach — before the search brief is written. Human-in-the-loop research, not an automated feed.
  </p>

  <h3 class="font-serif text-xl mt-12 mb-3">The watchlist</h3>
  <p class="font-serif text-base text-ink/85 leading-relaxed max-w-[640px] mb-3">
    {watchlistTotal} companies across five buckets — selected for active GTM hiring, no internal recruiting army, and a pattern that matches Betts's documented book.
  </p>
  <p class="font-serif italic text-base text-ink/90 max-w-[640px] mb-1">
    The methodology evolves when the data demands it.
  </p>
  <p class="text-xs text-muted leading-relaxed max-w-[640px] mb-6">
    Current as of April 27, 2026. Twelve companies (in <span class="italic">italic</span>) were added for Week 17 — the first scan against the prior 43-company list returned nothing, so the list expanded to surface four real launches at scaling AI-native customer-experience companies.
  </p>

  <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-x-10 gap-y-6 mb-12">
    {watchlist.map((b) => (
      <div>
        <p class="text-[10px] uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-accent mb-2 font-semibold">{b.label} · {b.companies.length}</p>
        <p class="font-serif text-base text-ink/85 leading-relaxed">
          {b.companies.map((c, i) => (
            <>
              {i > 0 && ' · '}
              <span class={c.addedW17 ? 'italic text-ink/60' : ''}>{c.name}</span>
            </>
          ))}
        </p>
      </div>
    ))}
  </div>

  <h3 class="font-serif text-xl mt-12 mb-4">Recent editions</h3>
  <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-4">
    {briefings.map((b) => (
      <a href={b.pdf} target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="block border border-rule rounded p-5 hover:border-accent transition bg-white">
        <p class="text-[10px] uppercase tracking-[0.15em] text-muted mb-2">Week {b.week} · {b.year} · {b.dateRange}</p>
        <p class="font-serif text-lg leading-snug">{b.summary}</p>
        <p class="text-xs text-accent mt-3 uppercase tracking-[0.12em]">Open PDF →</p>
      </a>
    ))}
  </div>

  <h3 class="font-serif text-xl mt-12 mb-4">Memo &amp; methodology</h3>
  <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-4">
    <a href={memo.pdf} target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="block border border-rule rounded p-5 hover:border-accent transition bg-white">
      <p class="text-[10px] uppercase tracking-[0.15em] text-muted mb-2">One-pager</p>
      <p class="font-serif text-lg leading-snug">{memo.title}</p>
      <p class="text-sm text-ink/75 mt-2">{memo.summary}</p>
      <p class="text-xs text-accent mt-3 uppercase tracking-[0.12em]">Open PDF →</p>
    </a>
    <a href={methodology.pdf} target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="block border border-rule rounded p-5 hover:border-accent transition bg-white">
      <p class="text-[10px] uppercase tracking-[0.15em] text-muted mb-2">How it's built</p>
      <p class="font-serif text-lg leading-snug">{methodology.title}</p>
      <p class="text-sm text-ink/75 mt-2">{methodology.summary}</p>
      <p class="text-xs text-accent mt-3 uppercase tracking-[0.12em]">Open PDF →</p>
    </a>
  </div>

  <h3 class="font-serif text-xl mt-12 mb-4">How I built it</h3>
  <p class="font-serif text-lg text-ink/85 leading-relaxed max-w-[640px]">
    GTM Radar is human-in-the-loop by design. I use Claude as a research partner — scanning the watchlist, scoring signals against a hiring-likelihood rubric, and drafting the recruiter angle for each one. I edit every briefing myself so the voice stays mine. The rendering is a small Python script; the real product is the workflow.
  </p>
</div>
